  "notes": [
    "Reflexive compound of *poner* — follows the same irregular patterns throughout.",
    "Irregular yo present: *me propongo* (go-verb), same pattern as *poner→pongo*.",
    "Irregular preterite stem: *propus-* (me propuse, te propusiste, se propuso...).",
    "Irregular future/conditional stem: *propondr-* (me propondré, me propondría).",
    "Subjuntivo built from the yo stem: *propong-* (me proponga, te propongas...).",
    "Irregular past participle, inherited from *poner→puesto*: **propuesto**.",
    "Imperativo tú affirmative is irregular, following *poner→pon*: *proponte* (not \"propónte\" — stress falls naturally on the default penultimate syllable, so no accent is needed). Usted/nosotros/ustedes affirmative forms attach the reflexive pronoun to the subjuntivo form with a written accent to preserve stress (propóngase, propongámonos, propónganse); negative forms place the pronoun separately in front (no te propongas...).",
    "*Se propuso terminar el proyecto antes de fin de mes.* (\"She set out to finish the project before the end of the month.\")",
    "*Nos propusimos aprender español este año.* (\"We set out to learn Spanish this year.\")",
    "Related: *proponer* (non-reflexive, \"to propose/suggest\"), *la propuesta* (proposal, noun), *plantearse* (near-synonym, \"to consider doing\")."
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/p/Proponerse.md"
